$$
\Delta_{o} \propto \frac{1}{\lambda}
$$
Therefore, the order of absorb wavelength is inversely proportional to the crystal field splitting energy (\(\Delta_o\)). The spectrochemical series for the ligands involved is \(Cl^- < H_2O < NH_3 < CN^-\). Thus, the order of \(\Delta_o\) (increasing) is:
[Co(NH_{3})_{5}(Cl)]^{2+} < [Co(NH_{3})_{5}(H_{2}O)]^{3+} < [Co(NH_{3})_{6}]^{3+} < [Co(CN)_{6}]^{3-}
Reversing this order for wavelength maxima (\(\lambda_{max}\)):
[Co(CN)_{6}]^{3-} < [Co(NH_{3})_{6}]^{3+} < [Co(NH_{3})_{5}H_{2}O]^{3+} < [Co(NH_{3})_{5}Cl]^{2+}
